<%# Which meals the badge gets, in both Table View and Edit Mode.

    Read-only in both: meals come from the person's provisions, not from the
    badge, so they are never a field in the bulk form. The wrapper carries a
    stable id so a provision change can replace this one cell with a
    turbo_stream, and Edit Mode adds a button that opens the provision dialog.

    Nothing in here is a form field, deliberately: the cell sits inside the
    bulk-edit form, and an input would let a provision change mark the badge
    row as edited.

    Locals:
      bmid       - the badge (saved or synthesized)
      provisions - the person's usable meals provisions, which is what the
                   label above is the union of. There can be more than one, so
                   the button opens the list of them rather than any one record
      editable   - Edit Mode, where the cell offers the provision dialog %>
<span id="<%= bmid_meals_cell_id(bmid) %>" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
  <span><%= bmid_meals_short_label(bmid) %></span>
  <% if local_assigns[:editable] %>
    <%= bmid_provision_cell_action(bmid, Provision::MEALS, local_assigns[:provisions]) %>
  <% end %>
</span>
